    <title>Useful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-02T00:37:33Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-1" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Testing yourself from memory strengthens recall more than simply rereading; after a page, close the book and see what you can explain in your own words.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#16dedb9ceaeae828aa3bedf1a22bcdbb40cbae8894d8f55c77b03e7d231d7c28</id>
    <title>Hopeful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-02T00:37:33Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-2" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Community fridges show how neighbours and local groups can organise surplus food for people who need it, turning practical coordination into everyday support.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#4ae97e0687bba3a763b87b032480eff297d4f8e0d2ed3ce981a94aa3993074d5</id>
    <title>Action</title>
    <updated>2026-11-02T00:37:33Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-3" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Pick a book nearby, open to any page and read one paragraph aloud; then retell it in a single sentence, as if telling a friend.</div>
    </content>
